                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "871d51e7-b341-37ed-9ce2-ad1585a7b58f",
                        "entry_id": "41add640-03a7-32e5-8542-d0a91892833d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small spate; a slight inundation or a sprinkle of rain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bff05467-670b-43d0-b301-483facea0b7e",
                                "sense_id": "871d51e7-b341-37ed-9ce2-ad1585a7b58f",
                                "text": "The caal^([sic]) or dam of Bankend-Mill, (Fact 12,) pens the water […] consequently, if this were removed, and the channel above widened and deepended, […] the water might be reduced in dry seasons 4 feet within bank, which would render the meadows more firm and dry, and carry off small spattles of rain, without damaging the crops; but in the larger summer floods this improvement would avail but little,[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "632f6161-7a22-4016-ae7f-560f6201494d",
                                "sense_id": "871d51e7-b341-37ed-9ce2-ad1585a7b58f",
                                "text": "Both painters abjure movement—no blustery clouds or spattles of rain, few running or jumping humans. To be sure, dancers and horse-persons people Luke's \"The Rehearsal\" (1950, commissioned by Hewitt) but they are closer to figures in the mediaeval Bayeux Tapestry,[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
